==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|niwjaz|lang=gem-pro}}, whence also Old Saxon and Old High German {{term|niuwi|lang=osx}}, Old Frisian {{term|nie|nīe|lang=ofs}}, Old English {{term|neowe|nēowe|lang=ang}}, {{term|niwe|nīwe|lang=ang}} (English {{term|new|lang=en}}), Gothic {{term|𐌽𐌹𐌿𐌾𐌹𐍃|tr=niujis|lang=got}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{recons|néwos|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Adjective===
{{non-adj}}

